# Greek myth, as a knowledge base

A compact knowledge base of Greek myth, from Chaos to Heracles among the
gods: who is born of whom and according to whom, what happens and where it
is told, and when each god is first attested. Every table below is an HQL
cell that `hql render` runs.

The knowledge base is HQL modules under `lib/myth/` with their records
beside them. The Greek script is handled by the `greek` package, whose
functions are declared in HQL without a body and implemented in Rust, in
`greek/`. The documents:

- [[theogony]]: from Chaos to the rule of Zeus, in Hesiod's order, and where
  the sources disagree
- [[olympians]]: the gods of Olympus, their names, families, domains and
  myths
- [[heracles]]: the hero's descent from the first powers, his twelve
  labours and his death
- [[evidence]]: the gods on Linear B tablets, at sanctuaries and in texts
- [[wikipedia]]: the knowledge base's ids mapped to two external
  namespaces, Wikipedia's articles and Wikidata's items

## What it holds

```hql
import myth.kb
import myth.evidence

[
    {records: "beings", count: kb.beings() | size},
    {records: "accounts of a birth", count: kb.parentage() | size},
    {records: "myths", count: kb.myths() | size},
    {records: "works cited", count: kb.works() | size},
    {records: "Linear B attestations", count: evidence.tablets() | size},
    {records: "sites", count: evidence.sites() | size},
]
| Table(columns = ["records", "count"])
```
<!-- hql:output hash=dfc7dc154668 status=ok -->
| records               | count |
| --------------------- | ----- |
| beings                | 103   |
| accounts of a birth   | 98    |
| myths                 | 49    |
| works cited           | 17    |
| Linear B attestations | 14    |
| sites                 | 17    |
<!-- /hql:output -->

## Kinds of being

Each being has one kind. The primordial powers come into being first; the
Titans are the children of Uranus and Gaia; the elder races, the Cyclopes,
the Hundred-Handers, the Erinyes and the Giants, are born with them. Of the
gods, the twelve of the Parthenon frieze are marked `olympian`.

```hql
import myth.kb

type Kind { kind : String, count : Int, examples : String }

kb.beings()
| group(by = b => b.kind)
| map(g => Kind(kind = g.key, count = g.items | size, examples = g.items | take(4) | map(b => b.name) | join(", ")))
| sort(by = k => 0 - k.count)
| Table(columns = ["kind", "count", "examples"])
```
<!-- hql:output hash=411fef2dc7aa status=ok -->
| kind       | count | examples                                   |
| ---------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------ |
| deity      | 23    | Phorcys, Ceto, Callirhoe, Clymene          |
| mortal     | 23    | Pandora, Deucalion, Pyrrha, Iasus          |
| titan      | 16    | Oceanus, Coeus, Crius, Hyperion            |
| olympian   | 12    | Demeter, Hera, Poseidon, Zeus              |
| primordial | 10    | Chaos, Gaia, Tartarus, Eros                |
| monster    | 10    | Typhon, Echidna, Orthus, Cerberus          |
| hero       | 5     | Cadmus, Perseus, Heracles, Iolaus          |
| elder      | 4     | Cyclopes, Hundred-Handers, Erinyes, Giants |
<!-- /hql:output -->

## The sources

The works the knowledge base cites, oldest first. A date is the work's
approximate date of composition; Homer and Hesiod are both placed around
700 BCE, and which came first is not known.

```hql
import myth.kb

kb.works()
| sort(by = w => w.year)
| map(w => {author: w.author, work: w.title, date: w.dating})
| Table(columns = ["author", "work", "date"])
```
<!-- hql:output hash=51518ad0e80c status=ok -->
| author             | work                  | date                                        |
| ------------------ | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| Homer              | Iliad                 | late 8th or early 7th century BCE           |
| Homer              | Odyssey               | c. 700 BCE                                  |
| Hesiod             | Theogony              | c. 700 BCE                                  |
| Hesiod             | Works and Days        | c. 700 BCE                                  |
| Homeric Hymns      | Hymn to Demeter (2)   | late 7th or 6th century BCE                 |
| Homeric Hymns      | Hymn to Apollo (3)    | 7th–6th century BCE                         |
| Homeric Hymns      | Hymn to Hermes (4)    | late 6th or early 5th century BCE           |
| Pindar             | Nemean Odes           | Nemean 1, c. 476–469 BCE                    |
| Pindar             | Olympian Odes         | Olympian 7, 464 BCE                         |
| Aeschylus          | Prometheus Bound      | c. 460–430 BCE; the attribution is disputed |
| Sophocles          | Women of Trachis      | c. 450–425 BCE                              |
| Herodotus          | Histories             | c. 430 BCE                                  |
| Euripides          | Heracles              | c. 416 BCE                                  |
| Euripides          | Bacchae               | produced 405 BCE                            |
| Ovid               | Metamorphoses         | completed c. 8 CE                           |
| Pseudo-Apollodorus | Library               | 1st–2nd century CE                          |
| Pausanias          | Description of Greece | c. 155–180 CE                               |
<!-- /hql:output -->

## This vault

These documents are the cards of a HyperMarkdown vault, and a cell can
query the vault itself: each card, the cards it links to and the cards
that link to it.

```hql
cards
| sort(by = c => c.name)
| map(c => {
    card: c.name,
    title: c.title,
    links_to: c | uplinks | map(e => e.target) | distinct | sort | join(", "),
    linked_from: c | downlinks | map(e => e.source) | distinct | sort | join(", "),
  })
| Table(columns = ["card", "title", "links_to", "linked_from"])
```
<!-- hql:output hash=8fb7c078ce65 status=ok -->
| card      | title                                         | links_to                                           | linked_from                |
| --------- | --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| README    | Greek Gods: an HQL demo over a small ontology |                                                    |                            |
| evidence  | The evidence                                  |                                                    | heracles, index            |
| heracles  | Heracles                                      | evidence, wikipedia                                | index, wikipedia           |
| index     | Greek myth, as a knowledge base               | evidence, heracles, olympians, theogony, wikipedia |                            |
| olympians | The Olympians                                 | theogony, wikipedia                                | index, theogony, wikipedia |
| theogony  | From Chaos to Zeus                            | olympians                                          | index, olympians           |
| wikipedia | Wikipedia                                     | heracles, olympians                                | heracles, index, olympians |
<!-- /hql:output -->
